{
  "note": "Re-judged 2026-10-23 (independent auditor, after c5edaea8f3). RFC 9494 Section 4.3: \"The route SHOULD NOT be advertised to any neighbor from which the Long-Lived Graceful Restart Capability has not been received. The exception is described in Section 4.6.\" Section 4.6 lets stale routes go to internal neighbors only with NO_EXPORT attached and LOCAL_PREF zero. test/plugin/llgr-egress-state-unloaded.ci changed because bgp-gr now refuses to run forked: it runs bgp-gr in the daemon (internal gr { use bgp-gr }) attached to the source only, so the egress state is loaded and records no LLGR Capability for obsn, whose OPEN carries none. The assertion is unchanged: obsn, an iBGP RR client, must first receive 10.0.0.0/24 and then a second UPDATE containing NO_EXPORT (FFFFFF01). The source sends no COMMUNITY, so NO_EXPORT can only come from gr_egress.go LLGREgressFilter, whose state-loaded branch (hasLLGR false, dest.PeerAS == dest.LocalAS) adds NO_EXPORT and sets LOCAL_PREF 0. The carrier now exercises the case the sentence names (a neighbor the capability was not received from, under a running daemon) rather than a process with no state at all, which is closer to the requirement; the nil-state branch keeps its unit TestLLGREgressFilter_NilStateWithdrawsEBGP. The Go units under this row are unchanged. No discrimination record exists for the .ci and this auditor could not run a single .ci; its green under the new arrangement rests on c5edaea8f3, and the plugin functional suite is owed by the main thread. Verdict stands.",
  "requirement_sha": "76231582d0f155d2",
